// audit-ci configuration — gate CI on npm audit with a documented allowlist
// for known vulnerabilities that cannot be fixed without a major upgrade.
//
// Policy:
//   - `high` and `critical` severities block CI.
//   - `skip-dev` limits the audit to production dependencies.
//   - `allowlist` entries MUST include: reason, tracked-debt ticket, expiry.
//
// Review cadence: every 90 days or whenever a new allowlist entry is added,
// whichever comes first. Entries past their expiry should be re-evaluated
// and either removed (upstream fixed), replaced with a concrete fix, or
// extended with fresh justification.
//
// 2026-09-15 re-triage — the allowlist went 15 entries → 1:
//   `npm audit fix` (non-breaking) resolved the whole v0.2.0 batch:
//     lodash 4.17.23→4.18.1, path-to-regexp 8.3.0→8.4.2, fast-uri 3.1.0→4.1.4,
//     react-router 7.13.1→7.18.3, ws 8.18.3→8.21.3, brace-expansion 1.1.13→1.1.21.
//   @nestjs/swagger moved 11.2.6→11.4.7, which finally unblocked the exact-pin
//   deadlock tracked in D-020 — so the lodash and path-to-regexp entries are gone.
//   @fastify/static moved ^9.0.0→^10.1.3 to match @nestjs/platform-fastify 11.2.4
//   (11.2.4 requires ^10.1.2; the old ^9 range silently broke SwaggerModule
//   static serving), which cleared its two advisories as a side effect.
//   Prod high+ advisories: 21 → 1.
{
  "$schema": "https://github.com/IBM/audit-ci/raw/main/docs/schema.json",
  "high": true,
  "critical": true,
  "skip-dev": true,
  "report-type": "summary",
  //
  // NOTE: audit-ci dedupes advisories per package, so one GHSA ID per
  // affected package is enough to cover the complementary advisory listed
  // on that same package by `npm audit`.
  "allowlist": [
    // ─── @opentelemetry/* — Prometheus exporter crash on malformed request ───
    // Path: @opentelemetry/auto-instrumentations-node → instrumentation-http /
    //       sdk-node → exporter-prometheus.
    // No non-breaking fix: the patched line requires an auto-instrumentations-node
    // bump past 0.76.0, which `npm audit fix` cannot reach without --force.
    // Exploitability is low in this codebase — the metrics port is internal-only and
    // not exposed through the public ingress, so a malformed request has to originate
    // from inside the trust boundary already.
    // Revisit when the @opentelemetry/* line is next upgraded.
    // Expiry: 2026-12-14 (90-day review per policy).
    "GHSA-q7rr-3cgh-j5r3", // @opentelemetry/*: exporter crash via malformed request
  ],
}
